   "info": "Alexander Wittek's City Hall of 1896, in the pseudo-Moorish style the Austrians thought fitting for Bosnia. From here Franz Ferdinand drove to his death in 1914. It was the National and University Library when it was shelled with incendiaries on the night of 25 August 1992: two million books burned, and the ash fell on the city for days. Rebuilt, it reopened in 2014."
  },
  {
   "name": "The Latin Bridge",
